# Round 19 (writer 10): settled; was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.9. GD-24: L §5.9 and §8.1 "`<b>: no row holds <x>` read with no law date". The old comment:
# MC-X-F12 (writer 9): rate isn't law-dated, so r reads it with no law date (L §4.3 rule 2), and no row holds 30.
# L §5.9 and §8.1 give the question `<b>: no row holds <x> at <law date>` and no form without a law date (the
# gap rule's `no value` form, L §4.6 step 5, is for a read with no candidate): REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED (q). Read
# at a law date, by a def with its own at (q2) or an ask line with law (q3), it is that hole.
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"

input age: int
band rate(a: int): money PLN
def r[m in months]: money PLN = rate(age)
def r2[m in months]: money PLN = rate(age) at start_of(m)
ask q: r[2027-05]
ask q2: r2[2027-05]
ask q3: rate(age) law 2027-05-01

version v_act
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  age = 30 "the age"
  rate: [0, 6) = 400.00 PLN "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"
=== expect
q: ?"rate: no row holds 30" (rate)
  cut 2027-12-31
q2: ?"rate: no row holds 30 at 2027-05-01" (rate)
  cut 2027-12-31
q3: ?"rate: no row holds 30 at 2027-05-01" (rate)
  law date 2027-05-01, cut 2027-12-31
